00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:34.120
communicates selecting various
pictures and exchange it with you.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.000
So they're communicating that way.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.610
Zoe: Social stories.

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:42.310
So using visual stories that
explain to a child a situation.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.960
Phil: We also use a lot of
AAC, so Augmentative and

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:49.340
Alternative Communication.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:55.440
So it might be an iPad and a more
high-tech version of a PECS book with

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.857
various symbols, touch the screen
and it verbalises what the symbol

00:01:00.752 --> 00:01:04.099
Zoe: The other thing quite related to
that would be comic strip conversations.

00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:08.567
So that's another way of explaining
a situation to a child with autism.

00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:12.470
It encourages you to look at the
situation from lots of different

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.050
perspectives and help them understand
how other people are thinking and

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.589
